   * Other half (18 guests) could have 1 hot dog
   * Total hot dogs prepared = (18 × 2) + (18 × 1)
   * Total hot dogs prepared = 36 + 18 = 54 hot dogs

2. Calculate how many hot dogs were needed:
   * 40 guests actually came
   * All wanted 2 hot dogs
   * Total hot dogs needed = 40 × 2 = 80 hot dogs

3. Calculate how many guests didn't get a second hot dog:
   * Hot dogs available = 54
   * First round used 40 hot dogs (one for each guest)
   * Remaining hot dogs = 54 - 40 = 14 hot dogs
   * Number of guests who got seconds = 14
   * Number who didn't get seconds = 40 - 14 = 26 guests

