"There are 30 students in Marissa’s class. Each student started the year with 10 pencils. After two months, 1/5 of the total pencils in class were unfortunately used. At the end of the year, only 1/3 of the remaining pencils were left. How many pencils were left?","There are 30 students in Marissa’s class. Each student started the year with 10 pencils. After two months, 1/5 of the total pencils in class were used. At the end of the year, only 1/3 of the remaining pencils were left. How many pencils were left?",80,80,80,80,"Let me solve this step by step.

1. Find the total number of pencils at the start:
* 30 students × 10 pencils = 300 pencils initially

2. Calculate how many pencils were left after two months:
* 1/5 of pencils were used
* 4/5 of pencils remained
* 300 × 4/5 = 240 pencils remained after two months

3. Calculate how many pencils were left at the end of the year:
* 1/3 of the remaining pencils were left
* 240 × 1/3 = 80 pencils

